      "authoringHints": {
        "styles": "Every style falls back to the app theme, so set only what the design needs to blend in (its accent, surfaces, borders and text colours), taking colours from the app theme or brand, never the defaults of another product. Radii and sizes are px. Styles are the way to restyle a pack widget: a cssClass only takes effect with workspace Custom styles, and Tailwind class names the pack does not already use are not compiled, so do not rely on either; for a one-off visual a style cannot express, use an Html component. Bind loadingState to the query's isLoading (each widget draws a skeleton or spinner in its own shape); tooltip shows on hover.",
        "usage": "A conversation: an assistant, a support thread, a team or customer chat, a care team, in place of a Table of messages or Html bubbles. initialChat is the history: an array of { message, type, name, avatar, timestamp, messageId } with type 'message' for this app's user (right) and 'response' for the other side (left). Bound to a messages query, map its rows: {{(queries.getMessages.data || []).filter(m => m.thread_id === variables.threadId).map(m => ({ message: m.body, type: m.sender === 'agent' ? 'message' : 'response', name: m.author, timestamp: m.sent_at, messageId: 'msg-' + m.id }))}}; a new value (another thread picked, the query refreshed) replaces the history. userName and userAvatar, respondentName and respondentAvatar name the two sides when a message has no name. Sending fires onMessageSent with the text in components.<chat>.lastMessage.message (lastMessage is the whole message object, so save .message, not lastMessage, in a text column). Wire onMessageSent to the save or AI query; on that query's success run the appendHistory action ({{ { message: <reply text>, type: 'response', name: <sender> } }}) or refresh the history query, with setResponseLoading true before and false after (a typing indicator), and setError on failure. A RunJS query can drive it in one place: await components.<chat>.setResponseLoading(true); await queries.save.run(); await components.<chat>.appendHistory({ message, type: 'response' }); await components.<chat>.setResponseLoading(false). loadingHistory shows the history loading, disableInput blocks sending (with emptyText and placeholder saying why, such as before a check-in is done). Replies render markdown (lists, bold, tables); the user's own turns are plain text. Set chatTitle '' and both header buttons off (enableClearHistoryButton, enableDownloadHistoryButton) when a card title already names it, or the header is an empty band. Fixed height (the messages scroll inside): 420 to 640px, a card, a page column or a side sheet; never fake chat bubbles with Text or Html."
      }
